WGARP Lean formalization
Source: https://github.com/vaguiarl/wgarp-lean

Mathematical attribution
The mathematical results formalized in this package are from
"A Rationalization of the Weak Generalized Axiom of Revealed Preference"
by Victor H. Aguiar, Per Hjertstrand, Roberto Serrano, and Özgür Evren,
and the classical revealed-preference literature identified in the sources.
The mathematical proofs were developed by the authors. The Lean files
provide supplementary machine verification; this notice does not attribute
authorship of every Lean proof to every mathematical author.

The infinite-data Afriat result is Philip J. Reny's (2015),
"A Characterization of Rationalizable Consumer Behavior", Econometrica
83(1), 175--192, doi:10.3982/ECTA12345. The logical-compactness scaling
approach and its prescribed-gap proof architecture are due to Yannai A.
Gonczarowski, Scott Duke Kominers, and Ran I. Shorrer (2025), "To infinity
and beyond: A general framework for scaling economic theories",
Theoretical Economics 20(2), 511--542, doi:10.3982/TE5878. These are prior
results of those authors, not new economic theorems of the WGARP authors.
The Lean implementation uses Mathlib compactness and a finite scalar
normalization of utilities; it does not reproduce every source proof step.

